   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `delete INDEX`, and `python tools/check.py` now passes: 5 tests, and the line-length check is clean.\n\n**Red:** I wrote the tests first and ran `check.py` with `NOTES_HOME` set to a temp directory, which the script requires. Three of the five tests failed, as expected:\n- Two errored with `AttributeError: module 'fieldnotes.store' has no attribute 'delete'`.\n- One failed because the CLI returned 2 for `delete` instead of 0.\n\n**Green:**\n- `fieldnotes/store.py`: new `delete(index)` removes and returns the note at that position. It raises `IndexError` if the index is out of range.\n- `fieldnotes/cli.py`: new `delete INDEX` command that prints `deleted: <text>`. A non-numeric or out-of-range index prints an error to stderr and returns 2. I also pulled the usage string into a `USAGE` constant that now mentions `delete`.\n- `tests/test_store.py`: tests for the store function, the CLI command and the bad-index cases.\n\n**`INDEX` is 1-based.** `list` doesn't print numbers, so I had to pick a convention, and 1-based is what users would count. If you'd rather have 0-based, or have `list` show the numbers, say so and I'll change it.",
