   "reply": "I added a `count` command that prints the number of notes, and the project checks now pass (6 tests OK, line-length check clean).\n\n- **Command:** `fieldnotes/cli.py` handles `count` with no extra arguments. It prints `len(store.load())`, and `0` when there are no notes. I also added `count` to the usage string and the module docstring.\n- **Test:** `test_count_command` in `tests/test_store.py` checks that `count` prints `0` on an empty store and `2` after adding two notes.\n- **Checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set, so I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory. The first run failed the 100-character line limit because my longer docstring went over, so I shortened it and the second run passed.",
